.TH NNI\-SPLASH 8 "2026-11-09" "nni @VERSION@" "nni family manual"
.SH NAME
nni\-splash \- draw a picture on the Linux framebuffer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nni\-splash
.I IMAGE.ppm
.RI [ DEVICE ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Fills the screen with the picture's top\-left colour and draws the picture
in the middle, enlarged by a whole number when the screen has room. The
boot script uses it to show the chicken while booting (setting SPLASH in
.BR nni.conf (5)).
The picture must be a binary PPM (P6, 255 levels). The device defaults to
.IR /dev/fb0 ;
16, 24 and 32 bits per pixel are supported.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NNI_SPLASH_TEST
.RI \(dq "WIDTH HEIGHT BPP FILE" \(dq
writes what would be drawn to FILE instead of a real framebuffer.
.SH FILES
.I /usr/share/nni/splash.ppm
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nni (8),
.BR nni.conf (5)
